From c5a0e0ae6df6ab91cfa17fabec2ff5401d877038 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael C. Ferguson" <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:48:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: host: keep the cadence of a periodic QH
 resubmitted in time

A full-speed interrupt IN endpoint with bInterval 1 on a full-speed root
port is polled only every other frame in buffer DMA mode: a 1 kHz HID
mouse delivers 500 reports/s, every gap about 2 ms.

The URB is given back through HCD_BH, after dwc2_hcd_qh_deactivate() has
moved next_active_frame to the next period and, with the qtd_list empty,
unlinked the QH. When the class driver resubmits, dwc2_schedule_periodic()
finds the reservation still pending and re-picks the start frame if
next_active_frame is not after the current frame. next_active_frame is
one frame before the QH goes on the wire, so it being the current frame
means the QH is exactly on time. For the transfer on the wire in frame N
that is next_active_frame == N, the usual case when the resubmit lands in
the same frame, and dwc2_pick_first_frame() then chooses N + 1, which
puts the next transfer on the wire in N + 2.

Only re-pick once the current frame has moved past next_active_frame.
The QH then keeps the cadence dwc2_next_periodic_start() computed, which
already accounts for EO misses, and a resubmit that is really late still
gets a fresh frame from dwc2_pick_first_frame().

The same off-by-one costs a period for any interval when the resubmit
lands in the frame (or high-speed microframe) that next_active_frame
names; with a 1 frame interval it happens on every poll.

Fixes: fb616e3f837e ("usb: dwc2: host: Manage frame nums better in scheduler")
Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_queue.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_queue.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_queue.c
index 3da952e..ad5137c 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_queue.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_queue.c
@@ -1322,9 +1322,12 @@ static int dwc2_schedule_periodic(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg, struct dwc2_qh *qh)
 		 * is still good.  Note: we could also try to use the similar
 		 * dwc2_next_periodic_start() but that schedules much more
 		 * tightly and we might need to hurry and queue things up.
+		 *
+		 * next_active_frame is one frame before our frame on the wire,
+		 * so it is still good while it is the current frame.
 		 */
-		if (dwc2_frame_num_le(qh->next_active_frame,
-				      dwc2_hcd_get_frame_number(hsotg)))
+		if (dwc2_frame_num_gt(dwc2_hcd_get_frame_number(hsotg),
+				      qh->next_active_frame))
 			dwc2_pick_first_frame(hsotg, qh);
 	}
 
